1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,485
A first trial lesson is a short first class.

2
00:00:03,485 --> 00:00:08,521
The teacher meets you, listens to your English, and learns what you need.

3
00:00:08,521 --> 00:00:12,394
You also learn about the teacher and the class style.

4
00:00:12,394 --> 00:00:15,880
Warm-up: Why do you want to study English now?

5
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:21,302
What is easy for you in English? What is difficult for you in English?

6
00:00:21,302 --> 00:00:24,014
When can you study during the week?

7
00:00:24,014 --> 00:00:27,887
What do you want the teacher to know about you?

8
00:00:27,887 --> 00:00:31,760
A trial lesson is not a test with a score.

9
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:36,408
It is a first meeting. The teacher may ask you simple questions.

10
00:00:36,408 --> 00:00:41,831
The teacher may ask you to read, listen, or speak for a short time.

11
00:00:41,831 --> 00:00:46,479
The teacher wants to understand your English. Are you comfortable with greetings?

12
00:00:46,479 --> 00:00:51,126
Can you talk about your day? Can you explain a simple idea?

13
00:00:51,126 --> 00:00:55,774
Can you understand slow questions? You can also learn about the class.

14
00:00:55,774 --> 00:01:07,007
You can ask, "How do lessons work?" You can ask, "Will I get homework?" You can ask, "Can we practice speaking more?" A good trial lesson helps both people.

15
00:01:07,007 --> 00:01:12,429
The teacher learns what to teach. The learner learns what the class feels like.

16
00:01:12,429 --> 00:01:15,528
Your goal is the reason you want English.

17
00:01:15,528 --> 00:01:18,239
A goal can be big or small.

18
00:01:18,239 --> 00:01:24,049
You may want English for travel, work, school, a test, a hobby, or daily conversation.

19
00:01:24,049 --> 00:01:26,373
Try to make your goal clear.

20
00:01:26,373 --> 00:01:30,634
"I want better English" is true, but it is very general.

21
00:01:30,634 --> 00:01:44,577
A clearer goal is, "I want to speak more comfortably when I travel." Another clear goal is, "I want to answer simple questions at work." If you do not know your goal yet, that is okay.

22
00:01:44,577 --> 00:01:52,324
You can say, "I am not sure yet, but I want to feel more confident." This is a useful answer.

23
00:01:52,324 --> 00:01:57,746
The teacher can help you find a goal. Many learners worry about their level.

24
00:01:57,746 --> 00:02:05,106
They think, "My English is too low," or "I will make mistakes." Mistakes are normal in a language class.

25
00:02:05,106 --> 00:02:08,204
You can describe your level with simple words.

26
00:02:08,204 --> 00:02:24,472
You can say, "I can understand slow English, but speaking is hard." You can say, "I know some grammar, but I need more practice." You can say, "I can read short texts, but listening is difficult." Do not hide your weak points.

27
00:02:24,472 --> 00:02:27,958
Your weak points are useful information for the teacher.

28
00:02:27,958 --> 00:02:32,606
If pronunciation is hard, say it. If listening is hard, say it.

29
00:02:32,606 --> 00:02:36,092
If grammar is confusing, say it. Your schedule matters.

30
00:02:36,092 --> 00:02:39,190
A strong plan must fit your real life.

31
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:43,451
If you are busy, do not promise two hours every day.

32
00:02:43,451 --> 00:02:46,162
Choose a plan you can really do.

33
00:02:46,162 --> 00:02:49,648
You can tell the teacher when you are available.

34
00:02:49,648 --> 00:03:03,979
For example, "I am free on Tuesday evenings." You can also say, "Weekends are better for me." If your schedule changes, you can say, "My work schedule is not always the same." Study habits are also important.

35
00:03:03,979 --> 00:03:06,690
A small habit can help a lot.

36
00:03:06,690 --> 00:03:09,789
Ten minutes of review after class is useful.

37
00:03:09,789 --> 00:03:13,275
Listening to the audio twice a week is useful.

38
00:03:13,275 --> 00:03:15,986
Speaking one answer out loud is useful.

39
00:03:15,986 --> 00:03:21,409
The best study plan is not always big. The best study plan is realistic.

40
00:03:21,409 --> 00:03:25,282
A teacher can help better when you explain your worry.

41
00:03:25,282 --> 00:03:29,930
You may feel nervous about speaking. You may be worried about pronunciation.

42
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:33,803
You may feel slow when you listen. Use simple sentences.

43
00:03:33,803 --> 00:03:44,261
"I feel nervous when I speak." "I need more time to answer." "Please speak slowly." "Can you correct me after I finish?" These sentences are not weak.

44
00:03:44,261 --> 00:03:47,747
They are smart. They help the class work better.

45
00:03:47,747 --> 00:03:52,395
You can also tell the teacher what kind of correction you like.

46
00:03:52,395 --> 00:03:57,430
Some learners want correction right away. Some learners want to finish speaking first.

47
00:03:57,430 --> 00:03:58,979
Both styles can work.

48
00:03:58,979 --> 00:04:04,402
Feedback is advice about what you did well and what you can improve next.

49
00:04:04,402 --> 00:04:09,050
Teacher: Welcome. Is this your first trial lesson? Learner: Yes, it is.

50
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:14,472
I feel a little nervous, but I am ready. Teacher: That is completely fine.

51
00:04:14,472 --> 00:04:17,571
Why do you want to study English now?

52
00:04:17,571 --> 00:04:22,606
Learner: I want to speak more comfortably when I travel. Teacher: Good goal.

53
00:04:22,606 --> 00:04:25,318
What feels easy for you in English?

54
00:04:25,318 --> 00:04:30,353
Learner: Reading short texts is okay for me. Teacher: And what feels difficult?

55
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:35,775
Learner: Listening is difficult. I also need more time to answer. Teacher: Thank you.

56
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:38,487
When are you usually available for lessons?

57
00:04:38,487 --> 00:04:43,134
Learner: I am available on Tuesday evenings and Saturday mornings. Teacher: Great.

58
00:04:43,134 --> 00:04:45,846
Do you have a study habit now?

59
00:04:45,846 --> 00:04:51,268
Learner: I listen to short English videos, but I do not practice speaking much.

60
00:04:51,268 --> 00:04:54,367
Teacher: We can build a small speaking habit.

61
00:04:54,367 --> 00:04:59,789
Could you practice three answers after each class? Learner: Yes, I can do that.

62
00:04:59,789 --> 00:05:04,050
Please correct my pronunciation after I finish speaking. Practice this roleplay.

63
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:09,473
Then change one detail: the goal, the schedule, the worry, or the homework plan.

64
00:05:09,473 --> 00:05:14,508
QUESTION 1: Is a trial lesson only a test? ### Comprehension Answer No.

65
00:05:14,508 --> 00:05:16,444
It is a first meeting.

66
00:05:16,444 --> 00:05:20,705
The teacher checks your English, and you learn about the class.

67
00:05:20,705 --> 00:05:23,804
QUESTION 2: Why is a clear goal helpful?

68
00:05:23,804 --> 00:05:29,226
### Comprehension Answer A clear goal helps the teacher choose useful practice for you.

69
00:05:29,226 --> 00:05:33,874
QUESTION 3: Should you hide your weak points in a trial lesson?

70
00:05:33,874 --> 00:05:38,909
### Comprehension Answer No. Weak points help the teacher understand what you need.

71
00:05:38,909 --> 00:05:43,170
DISCUSSION 4: What small study habit can you do this week?

72
00:05:43,170 --> 00:05:46,269
QUESTION 5: Why should you explain your worry?

73
00:05:46,269 --> 00:05:51,304
### Comprehension Answer The teacher can choose better help and correction for you.

74
00:05:51,304 --> 00:05:56,726
Speaking Practice Questions 1. What is your English goal for the next three months?

75
00:05:56,726 --> 00:06:00,212
2. What can you already do in English? 3.

76
00:06:00,212 --> 00:06:04,086
What is one weak point you want to improve? 4.

77
00:06:04,086 --> 00:06:07,571
When are you available for lessons or practice? 5.

78
00:06:07,571 --> 00:06:09,895
What kind of correction helps you?

79
00:06:09,895 --> 00:06:13,769
Before a trial lesson, you do not need perfect English.

80
00:06:13,769 --> 00:06:19,191
You need clear and honest answers. A good answer helps the teacher understand you.

81
00:06:19,191 --> 00:06:22,290
A good question helps you understand the class.

82
00:06:22,290 --> 00:06:27,712
Prepare your goal, your level, your schedule, your worry, and one small study habit.

83
00:06:27,712 --> 00:06:32,360
Then your first trial lesson can feel less scary and more useful.
